WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Council Tax is a local tax on your home, collected by your council. It depends on your home's band (A to H in England, based on its value in 1991), on what your council charges and on your discounts.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Usually adults aged 18 or over pay. Couples who live together are jointly responsible. In Wales the bands go from A to I. In Northern Ireland there is no Council Tax: there is another system («rates»).

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Find your council with your postcode and register as soon as you move in, with the date you moved in. When you move, tell the council you are leaving and the new one. Do not assume the landlord always pays: it depends on the contract. Ask in writing.

4
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.200
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
